--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/iterations/036-ds-catchup-member-management-and-auth/preview-conventions.md
@@ -0,0 +1,156 @@
+# DS preview conventions
+
+Task 002 confirmation for where this iteration's repo-side DS previews live and what each self-contained preview head must include.
+
+## Repo location decision
+
+Use the preferred `design-system/` mirror directory for all new or changed preview deliverables in this iteration.
+
+Existing `spikes/ds-convert/` files remain useful reference material for the phase-2 daisyUI conversion style, but they are not the delivery location for this iteration. The mirror keeps the eventual DesignSync push mechanical: remove the `design-system/` prefix and push the same relative path into the cloud DS project.
+
+| Repo path | Cloud DS path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `design-system/wireframes/invite-a-member.html` | `wireframes/invite-a-member.html` | Invite-a-member preview, showing the member-admin and staff/admin variants together unless task 003 finds two sibling files render clearer. |
+| `design-system/wireframes/profile-completion.html` | `wireframes/profile-completion.html` | Invited-member profile completion preview. |
+| `design-system/wireframes/auth-check-email.html` | `wireframes/auth-check-email.html` | Sign-in check-email and auth delivery-progress preview. |
+| `design-system/components/badges/badges.card.html` | `components/badges/badges.card.html` | Badges component card with the role / Membership-Admin chips added. |
+
+If the invite variants are split during task 003 for readability, use sibling files under the same directory (`design-system/wireframes/invite-a-member-member-admin.html` and `design-system/wireframes/invite-a-member-staff.html`) with the same prefix-stripping mapping.
+
+## Relative asset paths
+
+Author paths as if `design-system/` is the DS root:
+
+- From `design-system/wireframes/*.html` to DS root assets: `../brand/...`.
+- From `design-system/components/badges/*.html` to DS root assets: `../../brand/...`.
+- Prefer inline SVGs, text marks, initials, or CSS-only marks where that is enough to mirror the shipped surface; do not point previews at Phoenix app static paths.
+- Do not link `styles.css`, `memba.css`, or the app build output. Each preview must carry the CDN links and CSS it needs.
+
+## Self-contained head block
+
+Paste this shape into each new preview and adjust only the `<title>` plus page-specific raw tokens/layout CSS. The `:root` variables are copied from `web/assets/css/app.css`; keep them in sync if the app theme changes.
+
+```html
+<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="utf-8">
+  <title>Preview title · Memba</title>
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Figtree:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap">
+
+  <!-- daisyUI component CSS, prebuilt — renders the app's daisyUI components with no build step. -->
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/daisyui@5">
+
+  <style>
+    /* Memba raw tokens (mirror of web/assets/css/app.css @theme). */
+    :root {
+      --color-sage-50:#eef1e6;
+      --color-sage-100:#dde3cf;
+      --color-sage-200:#bccaa6;
+      --color-sage-300:#98ab80;
+      --color-sage-400:#6f8760;
+      --color-sage-500:#5a7050;
+      --color-sage-600:#475a40;
+      --color-sage-700:#36462f;
+      --color-sage-800:#232e1e;
+
+      --color-cream:#f6f5ea;
+      --color-paper:#fffef9;
+      --color-apricot:#d2925a;
+      --color-apricot-soft:#f6e8d6;
+      --color-apricot-deep:#925f2e;
+
+      --color-ink:#25291d;
+      --color-ink-2:#555a47;
+      --color-ink-3:#878b76;
+
+      --color-line:#e8e6d4;
+      --color-line-strong:#d9d6bf;
+      --color-success:#5f7a4f;
+      --color-warning:#a8772e;
+      --color-error:#a8503a;
+      --color-info:#4f6b78;
+      --color-success-soft:#e9eedd;
+      --color-warning-soft:#f3ecd8;
+      --color-error-soft:#f1ddd3;
+      --color-info-soft:#e3e9ec;
+
+      --font-sans:"Figtree",ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;
+      --font-mono:"JetBrains Mono",ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;
+    }
+
+    /* daisyUI "light" theme — copied from web/assets/css/app.css. */
+    :root {
+      color-scheme:light;
+      --color-base-100:#fffef9;
+      --color-base-200:#f6f5ea;
+      --color-base-300:#e8e6d4;
+      --color-base-content:#25291d;
+      --color-primary:#5a7050;
+      --color-primary-content:#f6f5ea;
+      --color-secondary:#555a47;
+      --color-secondary-content:#f6f5ea;
+      --color-accent:#d2925a;
+      --color-accent-content:#25291d;
+      --color-neutral:#25291d;
+      --color-neutral-content:#f6f5ea;
+      --color-info:#4f6b78;
+      --color-info-content:#f6f5ea;
+      --color-success:#5f7a4f;
+      --color-success-content:#f6f5ea;
+      --color-warning:#a8772e;
+      --color-warning-content:#f6f5ea;
+      --color-error:#a8503a;
+      --color-error-content:#f6f5ea;
+      --radius-selector:0.375rem;
+      --radius-field:0.375rem;
+      --radius-box:0.75rem;
+      --size-selector:0.25rem;
+      --size-field:0.25rem;
+      --border:1px;
+      --depth:0;
+      --noise:0;
+    }
+
+    * { box-sizing:border-box; }
+    html, body { margin:0; }
+    body {
+      min-height:100vh;
+      background:var(--color-base-200);
+      color:var(--color-base-content);
+      font-family:var(--font-sans);
+      -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
+      text-rendering:optimizeLegibility;
+    }
+
+    /* Page-specific layout CSS goes here. Use plain CSS, not Tailwind utilities. */
+  </style>
+</head>
+```
+
+## Class-mapping rules
+
+Use daisyUI components plus plain CSS. Do not rely on Tailwind utility classes in these static CDN previews; the phase-2 spike showed they silently fail without the app build.
+
+| Bespoke / app pattern | Static preview pattern |
+| --- | --- |
+| `btn btn--primary` | `btn btn-primary` |
+| `btn btn--secondary` | `btn btn-soft` |
+| `btn btn--ghost` | `btn btn-ghost` |
+| `btn btn--color-error` | `btn btn-error` |
+| `btn--lg` / `btn--sm` | `btn-lg` / `btn-sm` |
+| `pill p-ok` | `badge badge-success badge-soft` |
+| `pill p-info` | `badge badge-info badge-soft` |
+| `pill p-warn` | `badge badge-warning badge-soft` |
+| `pill p-bad` | `badge badge-error badge-soft` |
+| `statpill--ok` / `spill--active` | `badge badge-success badge-soft` |
+| `statpill--bad` / `spill--paused` | `badge badge-warning badge-soft` |
+| `spill--trial` | `badge badge-info badge-soft` |
+| `spill--bounced` | `badge badge-error badge-soft` |
+| `role role--lead/base/safe` | `badge` plus primary/neutral/info soft variants, or a small CSS-only role-chip wrapper if needed for fidelity. |
+| `input` / `textarea` | daisyUI `input` / `textarea` |
+| `field` / `field__label` / `field__hint` | `fieldset`, `label`, `fieldset-label`, or equivalent plain CSS when a shipped app form needs exact spacing. |
+| `av` / `av--sm` / `av--lg` | `avatar avatar-placeholder` only if it renders via daisyUI CDN; otherwise plain CSS initials circles. |
+
+For layout, write local classes such as `.invite-shell`, `.profile-card`, or `.progress-step` in the preview `<style>` block instead of Tailwind utilities like `flex`, `gap-4`, `w-full`, `text-sm`, or `rounded-xl`.
